  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 400 F. Set a rack in the middle.",
    "Warm the olive oil in a 10 inch oven-safe skillet over medium-high heat. Add the mushrooms and onion and cook for 6 to 7 minutes, until the mushrooms are browned and the liquid is gone.",
    "Stir in the garlic for 30 seconds. Add the spinach in handfuls and cook for 2 minutes, until wilted.",
    "Whisk the eggs, milk, salt, pepper, and oregano in a large bowl until smooth. Stir in the mozzarella and half of the Parmesan.",
    "Pour the egg mixture into the skillet and stir once to spread the vegetables evenly. Sprinkle the rest of the Parmesan on top.",
    "Bake for 16 to 18 minutes, until the center is set and no longer jiggles, and the top is lightly golden.",
    "Rest for 5 minutes, then cut into 8 wedges. Cool leftovers, cover, and refrigerate for up to 4 days. Reheat in a 300 F oven or microwave until hot."
  ],
